# Where the Test Panel's Genotype Store (`genotype-store/`, beside this file) comes from.
#
# opengwasdb commits the store ogquery's Genotype Store reader reads in its own tests
# (opengwas/ogquery#11, ogquery ADR 0002, amended): ogquery holds the same bytes at the same path
# under `tests/ld/data/test-panel/genotype-store/`, listed in its `tests/ld/data/SOURCE`, whose
# block below is copied here verbatim. Each `output` line is a file of the store: its git blob id
# and its path. `tests/ld/test_genotype_store_source.py` holds the store to every line, holds each
# `input` line to the file of that blob committed here, and builds the store again with this
# repository's build, which is the same store but for the build record (when, how long, peak
# memory), the `software` versions and the ALID companion's generation, which hashes the root
# document and names its directory.
#
# The store pins `../panel.pgen`, `../panel.psam` and `../panel.pvar` (the files beside it) by
# size, mtime and SHA-256. Git keeps no mtime, so a test reads a copy whose inputs carry the
# recorded one (`tests/ld/genotype_fixture.py`), never the files here.
#
# Refresh by building it again at `generated-commit` or a later commit, from a `git archive` of
# it, and copying the result and the block from ogquery's refreshed SOURCE.

# Generated, not copied: the Test Panel's Genotype Store, which ogquery's Genotype Store reader
# reads (opengwas/ogquery#11; ADR 0002, amended). opengwasdb's tests build one in a scratch
# directory each session and commit none, so it was built once by opengwasdb 964ac1b2's own build,
# the command its tests/ld/conftest.py runs, from a `git archive` of that commit (tag v0.26.0) in
# its own pixi environment (pgenlib 0.95.2), in the archive's tests/ld/data/test-panel/:
#
#   pixi install --locked -e dev
#   SETUPTOOLS_SCM_PRETEND_VERSION=0.26.0 pixi reinstall -e dev opengwasdb
#   PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1 OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 MKL_NUM_THREADS=1 \
#       pixi run -e dev opengwasdb ld build --genotypes --pgen P/panel.pgen --keep P/panel.keep \
#       --pcs P/pcs.eigenvec --pc-source "Test Panel" --panel-id "Test Panel" --ancestry EUR \
#       --genotype-source "Test Panel" --r-scale 511 --t-partner 0.01 --info-min none \
#       P/genotype-store
#
# with P = tests/ld/data/test-panel. It pins its inputs by path relative to itself
# (`../panel.pgen`), size, mtime and SHA-256, and an open refuses a changed size or mtime. Git
# keeps no mtime: a `git archive` gives every file the commit's time, 1795726371 s, which is what
# the store records, and a test reads it from a copy whose inputs it sets to the recorded mtime
# (genotype_answers.place). panel.pgen and panel.psam are copied here with it; they, panel.pvar,
# and the PC File and keep list the store also records (`inputs`, which no read opens and this
# repository does not hold) are the same blobs at 964ac1b2 as at the commit above. Its bytes are
# the run's, except the root's `build` record (when, how long, peak memory) and the ALID
# companion's generation, which hashes the root document.
